    "result_text": "The full build passes. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `contactPreference` derived field on the owner API: it returns `EMAIL` when an owner has an email on file, otherwise `PHONE`.\n\nFollowing the existing `Locality` derivation pattern, I kept the logic small and in its proper place rather than adding it inline to the mapper:\n\n- **`model/ContactPreference.java`** (new) \u2014 a small final utility mirroring `Locality`, with `EMAIL`/`PHONE` constants and a `forOwner(Owner)` factory holding the single rule.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `hasEmail()` predicate (non-blank email check), so the \"email present\" notion lives on the entity.\n- **`service/MembershipLevelEvaluator.java`** \u2014 reused `Owner.hasEmail()`, removing its private duplicate of the same check.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added the `contactPreference` mapping expression, alongside the other derived fields.\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared `contactPreference` as a read-only string on the Owner schema (same style as `locality`), which regenerates the `OwnerDto` field at build time.\n\nTests: `AcceptanceTest` (both `corePhoneWhenNoEmail` and `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) pass, and the full `./mvnw test` build is green.",
